Include this platform's evdev UAPI header, and stop requiring libudev.

The header change is the same one-line redirect applied to libevdev and mtdev.

libudev is a different matter: configure demands it, but src/evdev.c uses it in
exactly one function -- EvdevDeviceIsVirtual(), which looks for "LNXSYSTM" in a
sysfs device path -- and that function is ALREADY wrapped in #ifdef
HAVE_LIBUDEV with a "return FALSE" fallback.  So the hard requirement buys
nothing: without udev the code compiles out and the driver works, but configure
refuses to get that far.  Made optional, which is what the source already
assumes.

configure.ac changes have no effect until `configure` is regenerated, so the
port deletes the shipped one; see unpack.sh.

--- a/src/evdev.h
+++ b/src/evdev.h
@@ -35,7 +35,13 @@
 #ifndef EVDEV_H
 #define EVDEV_H
 
+/* This platform's evdev UAPI header. Same event structure, event codes and
+ * ioctl encoding; it is only reached under a different name. */
+#ifdef __LIKEOS__
+#include <sys/input.h>
+#else
 #include <linux/input.h>
+#endif
 #include <sys/types.h>
 
 /* Tolerate prior #include <linux/input.h> */
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -45,7 +45,15 @@
 
 # Obtain compiler/linker options from server and required extensions
 PKG_CHECK_MODULES(XORG, [xorg-server >= 1.18] xproto [inputproto >= 2.1.99.3])
-PKG_CHECK_MODULES(UDEV, libudev, [AC_DEFINE(HAVE_LIBUDEV, 1,[libudev support])])
+dnl libudev is optional, not required.  src/evdev.c uses it in exactly one
+dnl function -- EvdevDeviceIsVirtual(), which looks for "LNXSYSTM" in a sysfs
+dnl device path -- and that function is already wrapped in #ifdef HAVE_LIBUDEV
+dnl with a "return FALSE" fallback.  Demanding the library to build a check
+dnl that compiles out anyway makes the driver unbuildable on any system without
+dnl udev, for no gain.
+PKG_CHECK_MODULES(UDEV, libudev,
+                  [AC_DEFINE(HAVE_LIBUDEV, 1,[libudev support])],
+                  [AC_MSG_NOTICE([libudev not found; virtual-device detection disabled])])
 
 PKG_CHECK_MODULES(LIBEVDEV, [libevdev >= 0.4])
 PKG_CHECK_MODULES(MTDEV, mtdev)
